<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's Movement for the Liberation of Angola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1956</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as MPLA</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's Movement for the Liberation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a> (MPLA) is an Angolan political party founded in the 1950s, which fought Portuguese rule from 1961 under Agostinho Neto. Backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and Cuban troops, it took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda">Luanda</a> and declared Angola's independence in November 1975, then fought a long civil war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unita">UNITA</a>. It has governed Angola ever since, under José Eduardo dos Santos and João Lourenço.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mpla.jpg" alt="People's Movement for the Liberation of Angola" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. E2m assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_MPLA.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
